From f2cbe1cc89c7d24e2cd085aff4b0bcbd44b2a4ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shreyansh Kaushik <smkaushi@ucsc.edu>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:23:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lightpath: GNOME virtual display capture, Linux NVENC
 split-frame, Mac client input, clipboard sharing

- capture = mutter: per-stream virtual monitor matching the client mode, zero-copy capture
- NVENC split-frame encoding on Linux, bitrate-aware preset
- route-MTU packet sizing; advertise the LAN address to clients paired over a VPN overlay
- PipeWire fixes (uninitialized state, renegotiation treated as a dead stream)
- Mac clients (lightpathClient=mac): macOS shortcut translation (src/mac_keymap.h) and
  pixel-precise touchpad scrolling through Mutter's remote desktop API
- clipboard sharing for paired clients: GET/POST /lightpath/clipboard (text, PNG)

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JSGYnegbZ8CEyDK2p2YTH2
