+### mac_shortcuts
+
+<table>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Description</td>
+        <td colspan="2">
+            Give Mac clients (Lightpath's Moonlight build identifies itself with `lightpathClient=mac`) macOS shortcut
+            semantics: Cmd+key acts as Ctrl+key (copy, paste, undo, find, new tab, ...), Cmd+click as Ctrl+click,
+            Cmd+Tab and Cmd+` switch windows, Cmd+Left/Right/Up/Down jump to line and document edges,
+            Cmd+Backspace deletes to the line start, Cmd+Space opens search, Cmd+H/M hide the window,
+            Cmd+[ and Cmd+] go back and forward, Option+arrows/Backspace/Delete work on words, and Option is Alt.
+            Shift and Ctrl pass through unchanged. Other clients are never affected.
+            <br>
+            On GNOME, Mac clients also get touchpad-quality scrolling: trackpad deltas are injected as finger scrolling
+            in logical pixels (1:1 with the fingers, kinetic scrolling where applications implement it).
+        </td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Default</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            enabled
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+    <tr>
+        <td>Example</td>
+        <td colspan="2">@code{}
+            mac_shortcuts = disabled
+            @endcode</td>
+    </tr>
+</table>
+
